rootNode.detailAuthoring.setComponent('main',html`<main class="page"><div class="eyebrow">From raw text through deployment</div><h1>Training turns text into model weights</h1><p>The common decoder-only language-model pipeline follows this sequence. Each stage produces the artifact used by the next.</p>
<section class="stage"><div class="num">1</div><div><h2>Prepare text</h2><p>Collect text with appropriate provenance and usage rights. Normalize, filter, and deduplicate it; keep evaluation data separate.</p><div class="out">Output: curated corpus</div></div></section><div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
<section class="stage"><div class="num">2</div><div><h2>Tokenize and batch</h2><p>Encode text as token IDs. Build context windows with shifted next-token targets and appropriate masks.</p><div class="out">Output: training sequences</div></div></section><div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
<section class="stage"><div class="num">3</div><div><h2>Pretrain</h2><p>A causal transformer predicts the next token. Measure prediction loss, backpropagate, update weights, and repeat across many batches.</p><div class="out">Output: base-model checkpoint + tokenizer</div></div></section><div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
<section class="stage"><div class="num">4</div><div><h2>Post-train · optional</h2><p>Train on desired instruction-response examples. Preference optimization may further adapt behavior using feedback.</p><div class="out">Output: model adapted to its intended use</div></div></section><div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
<section class="stage"><div class="num">5</div><div><h2>Evaluate, deploy, monitor</h2><p>Check quality, robustness, privacy, and harmful behavior. Validate serving optimizations, release with rollback, and monitor real usage.</p><div class="out">Output: versioned model service</div></div></section>
<p class="note">Evaluation happens throughout; failures can send work back to earlier stages. Next-token training does not guarantee factuality or reliable behavior. Normal inference uses weights without updating them; feedback can inform a later training run. This is a conceptual map, not a report of a training run.</p>
